9 L 168.21 61.69 L 168.64 61.68 L 169.07 61.73 L 169.49 61.37 L 169.92 61.21 L 170.35 60.99 L 170.78 61.07 L 171.2 61.12 L 171.63 61.16 L 172.06 60.54 L 172.48 60.6 L 172.91 60.47 L 173.34 60.81 L 173.76 60.54 L 174.19 60.32 L 174.62 60.15 L 175.04 60.4 L 175.47 60.76 L 175.9 60.95 L 176.33 61.24 L 176.75 62.01 L 177.18 62.13 L 177.61 62.05 L 178.03 62.16 L 178.46 62.44 L 178.89 62.66 L 179.31 62.36 L 179.74 63.57 L 180.17 63.59 L 180.59 63.58 L 181.02 63.41 L 181.45 63.35 L 181.88 63.36 L 182.3 63.29 L 182.73 63.71 L 183.16 62.6 L 183.58 63.19 L 184.01 63.14 L 184.44 63.15 L 184.86 62.69 L 185.29 62.73 L 185.72 62.85 L 186.14 62.84 L 186.57 62.84 L 187 62.7 L 187.43 62.36 L 187.85 62.43 L 188.28 62.66 L 188.71 62.62 L 189.13 61.93 L 189.56 62 L 189.99 62.4 L 190.41 62.39 L 190.84 62.84 L 191.27 62.59 L 191.7 62.37 L 192.12 62.37 L 192.55 62.32 L 192.98 61.57 L 193.4 61.69 L 193.83 61.7 L 194.26 60.94 L 194.68 61.37 L 195.11 61.51 L 195.54 61.68 L 195.96 61.55 L 196.39 61.52 L 196.82 61.36 L 197.25 62.09 L 197.67 62.24 L 198.1 62.83 L 198.53 62.21 L 198.95 62.2 L 199.38 62.13 L 199.81 63.02 L 200.23 63.03 L 200.66 62.45 L 201.09 62.63 L 201.51 62.73 L 201.94 62.7 L 202.37 62.84 L 202.8 62.7 L 203.22 62.69 L 203.65 62.14 L 204.08 62.4 L 204.5 62.45 L 204.93 62.4 L 205.36 62.4 L 205.78 62.4 L 206.21 62.4 L 206.64 62.31 L 207.06 62.17 L 207.49 62.33 L 207.92 62.31 L 208.35 62.35 L 208.77 62.47 L 209.2 62.4 L 209.63 63.02 L 210.05 62.8 L 210.48 62.95 L 210.91 62.88 L 211.33 63.06 L 211.76 63.16 L 212.19 63.3 L 212.62 63.17 L 213.04 64.13 L 213.47 64.09 L 213.9 64.02 L 214.32 63.97 L 214.75 63.59 L 215.18 63.68 L 215.6 64.47 L 216.03 64.72 L 216.46 64.56 L 216.88 64.63 L 217.31 64.61 L 217.74 64.71 L 218.17 64.63"></path></g><g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 97.8 5.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.52em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="7.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F3.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -12.65 -38.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.51em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="131.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F3.pic1.3" class="ltx_text">(c) Strong association</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.F3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Metric illustration on <span id="S5.F3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abalone</span>. <span id="S5.F3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Top row:</span> context spectra. <span id="S5.F3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bottom row:</span> black solid curves are <math id="S5.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> divided by <math id="S5.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>; red dashed curves are the actual downstream prediction error. We divide <math id="S5.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> to fit it in the same plot.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we empirically examine <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> on two datasets.
First, we apply the metric to the <span id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">abalone</span> dataset and use KNN as the context, similar to <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Implications for Scaling Laws ‣ 4 Optimality of the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
We adjust the association of the context by changing <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, we choose <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=150</annotation></semantics></math> (weak), <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=30</annotation></semantics></math> (moderate) and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=5</annotation></semantics></math> (strong).
We obtain the exact eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{{k_{X}^{+}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{{k_{X}^{+}}}</annotation></semantics></math> using kernel PCA.
In <a href="#S5.F3" title="In Derivation of the metric. ‣ 5.2 Task-agnostic Evaluation of Contexts ‣ 5 Context Evaluation ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we plot the spectra of the three contexts in the top row.
Then, in the bottom row, we compare <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> against the prediction error of the linear probe under different <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can see that when the association is weak or moderate, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> first decreases and then increases, which tracks the actual error.
However, when the association is too strong, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> monotonically decreases with <math id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and it cannot track the actual error.</p>
