<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a one-hot random vector.
Suppose the linear layer is unbiased, that is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if it extracts the top-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenspace of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\mathbb{I}}[a=a^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\mathbb{I}}[a=a^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda g)(a)=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda g)(a)=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If all classes have the same size, then the top-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are the same.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma will be very useful in the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the integral kernel operator of the following kernel</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x,x^{\prime})=\iint k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})P^{+}(a|x)P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime})dada^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x,x^{\prime})=\iint k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})P^{+}(a|x)P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime})dada^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a^{\prime})=\int h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(x^{\prime}|a^{\prime})dx^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a^{\prime})=\int h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(x^{\prime}|a^{\prime})dx^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int(T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})da^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int(T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})da^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(x^{\prime}|a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})dx^{\prime}da^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(x^{\prime}|a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})dx^{\prime}da^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dx^{\prime}da^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint h(x^{\prime})P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dx^{\prime}da^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int(\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a)P^{+}(a|x)da" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int(\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}h)(a)P^{+}(a|x)da</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iiint h(x^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})P^{+}(a|x)P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dada^{\prime}dx^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∭</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iiint h(x^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})P^{+}(a|x)P^{+}(a^{\prime}|x^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dada^{\prime}dx^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int h(x^{\prime})k(x,x^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dx^{\prime}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int h(x^{\prime})k(x,x^{\prime}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x^{\prime})dx^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we finish the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any fixed <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})=\mathbb{E}_{P^{+}}{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})=\mathbb{E}_{P^{+}}{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming, without loss of generality, that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}[\Phi_{i}\Phi_{j}]=\delta_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}[\Phi_{i}\Phi_{j}]=\delta_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise one can perform Gram-Schmidt process on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and change the value of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Thus, it amounts to minimizing</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle A,{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle A,{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\left\|{\bm{W}}\right\|}_{F}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle A,{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\left\|{\bm{W}}\right\|}_{F}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle A,{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}=(w_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq d_{A},1\leq j\leq d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}=(w_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq d_{A},1\leq j\leq d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial{\mathcal{R}}}{\partial w_{ij}}=2w_{ij}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial{\mathcal{R}}}{\partial w_{ij}}=2w_{ij}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that for a fixed <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes this loss should satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the minimizer of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> and notice that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant, it suffices to <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">maximize</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j}{\left[\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j}{\left[\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;A_{i}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2}){\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}{P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1})P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})dx_{1}da_{1}dx_{2}da_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2}){\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}{P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1})P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})dx_{1}da_{1}dx_{2}da_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2})\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})dx_{1}dx_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2})\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})dx_{1}dx_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint{\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∬</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint{\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint{\mathbb{I}}[a_{1}=a_{2}]P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∬</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint{\mathbb{I}}[a_{1}=a_{2}]P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is a minimizer of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> extracts the top-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining with <a href="#Thmtheorem18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs for Section ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> yields that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\mathbb{I}}[a=a^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\mathbb{I}}[a=a^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda g)(a)=\int g(a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})d{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda g)(a)=\int g(a^{\prime})k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})d{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a^{\prime})=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>, as desired.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">If all classes have the same size, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)\equiv c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)\equiv c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. Thus <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda g)(a)=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)=cg(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda g)(a)=g(a){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)=cg(a)</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}=cT_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}=cT_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> share the same top-<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setting of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, suppose the linear layer is biased. Then, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}_{\rm bal}(\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>bal</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}_{\rm bal}(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if it learns the contexture of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us first assume that the linear layer is unbiased, that is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any fixed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})=\mathbb{E}_{P^{+}}{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})=\mathbb{E}_{P^{+}}{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming, without loss of generality,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{i}\Phi_{j}\right]}=\delta_{ij};" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{i}\Phi_{j}\right]}=\delta_{ij};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">otherwise we can perform Gram-Schmidt process on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and change the value of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Thus it suffices to minimize</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}{\left\|{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle\frac{A}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}},{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left[\frac{{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle\frac{A}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}},{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left[\frac{{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\left\|{\bm{W}}\right\|}_{F}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle\frac{A}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}},{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left[\frac{{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\right]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\left\|{\bm{W}}\right\|}_{F}^{2}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left\langle\frac{A}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}},{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)\right\rangle}+\underset{A\sim{P_{\mathcal{A}}}}{\mathbb{E}}{\left[\frac{{\left\|A\right\|}_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}=(w_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq d_{A},1\leq j\leq d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}=(w_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq d_{A},1\leq j\leq d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial{\mathcal{R}}}{\partial w_{ij}}=2w_{ij}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial{\mathcal{R}}}{\partial w_{ij}}=2w_{ij}-2\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that for a fixed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the minimizer of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to maximize</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}^{\prime}=\sum_{i,j}{\left[\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}^{2}=\iint\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2})\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})dx_{1}dx_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∬</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}^{\prime}=\sum_{i,j}{\left[\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;\frac{A_{i}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(A)}}\Phi_{j}(X)\right]}^{2}=\iint\sum_{j}\Phi_{j}(x_{1})\Phi_{j}(x_{2})\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{1}){P_{\mathcal{X}}}(x_{2})dx_{1}dx_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint\frac{{\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{1}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{2})}}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint\frac{{\left\langle a_{1},a_{2}\right\rangle}}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{1}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{2})}}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\iint\frac{{\mathbb{I}}[a_{1}=a_{2}]}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{1}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{2})}}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∬</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\iint\frac{{\mathbb{I}}[a_{1}=a_{2}]}{\sqrt{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{1}){P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a_{2})}}P^{+}(a_{1}|x_{1})P^{+}(a_{2}|x_{2})da_{1}da_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\frac{P^{+}(a|x_{1})P^{+}(a|x_{2})}{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)}dy." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\frac{P^{+}(a|x_{1})P^{+}(a|x_{2})}{{P_{\mathcal{A}}}(a)}dy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is a minimizer of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> extracts the top-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{k}(x_{1},x_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that here the top-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions include <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
When we include the bias <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{b}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the linear layer, then this <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is covered by the bias term, so <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> will extract <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\cdots,\mu_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\cdots,\mu_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 8 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 8 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> minimizes <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> if and only if <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> extracts the top-<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> eigenspace of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P^{+}}\Lambda T_{P^{+}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the linear layer is unbiased (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{b}}={\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>), then <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\left\langle a,a^{\prime}\right\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\left\langle a,a^{\prime}\right\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>;
if it is biased (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{b}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be arbitrary), then <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\left\langle\tilde{a},\tilde{a^{\prime}}\right\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\Lambda}(a,a^{\prime})={\left\langle\tilde{a},\tilde{a^{\prime}}\right\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the unbiased linear model, the proof is similar to that of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Proof in ). ‣ 3.1 Supervised Learning: Label Context ‣ 3 Learning the Contexture ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Combining <a href="#A1.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs for Section ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs for Section ‣ Contextures: Representations from Contexts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> yields the desired result.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we consider a biased linear model. For a variable <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{z}=\mathbb{E}[Z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{z}=\mathbb{E}[Z]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}=z-\mathbb{E}[Z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}=z-\mathbb{E}[Z]</annotation></semantics></math> as its centered version.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any fixed <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}},{\bm{b}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{R}}(\Phi,{\bm{W}},{\bm{b}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)-{\bm{b}}\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.710em">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">P</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{X\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}{\mathbb{E}}\;\underset{A\sim P^{+}(\cdot|X)}{\mathbb{E}}\;{\left[{\left\|A-{\bm{W}}\Phi(X)-{\bm{b}}\right\|}_{2}^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
