<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2505.01557v1/association/knn_err_decay_rate.png" id="A6.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/278;" width="648" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A6.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Association level vs <math id="A6.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{err}_{d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>err</mtext><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{err}_{d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the decay rate <math id="A6.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the KNN context on the 28 datasets. A larger <math id="A6.F8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/N</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a lower association level, while a smaller <math id="A6.F8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/N</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a higher association level. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2505.01557v1/association/rbf_err_decay_rate.png" id="A6.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/278;" width="648" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A6.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Association level vs <math id="A6.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{err}_{d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>err</mtext><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{err}_{d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the decay rate <math id="A6.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the RBF context on the 28 datasets. A larger <math id="A6.F9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a higher association level, while a smaller <math id="A6.F9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a higher association level.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2505.01557v1/association/knn_kernel_deviation_lipschitz.png" id="A6.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/278;" width="648" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A6.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Association level vs the kernel deviation <math id="A6.F10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}|{k_{X}^{+}}(x,x^{\prime})-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}|{k_{X}^{+}}(x,x^{\prime})-1|</annotation></semantics></math> and the Lipschitz constant <math id="A6.F10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the KNN context on the 28 datasets. A larger <math id="A6.F10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/N</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a lower association level, while a smaller <math id="A6.F10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/N</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a higher association level. We multiply <math id="A6.F10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the input feature dimension <math id="A6.F10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{feat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{feat}</annotation></semantics></math> to normalize the <math id="A6.F10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance in the denominator. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2505.01557v1/association/rbf_kernel_deviation_lipschitz.png" id="A6.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/278;" width="648" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A6.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Association level vs the kernel deviation <math id="A6.F11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}|{k_{X}^{+}}(x,x^{\prime})-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}\sim{P_{\mathcal{X}}}}|{k_{X}^{+}}(x,x^{\prime})-1|</annotation></semantics></math> and the Lipschitz constant <math id="A6.F11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the RBF context on the 28 datasets. A larger <math id="A6.F11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> indicates a higher association level, while a smaller <math id="A6.F11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a higher association level. We multiply <math id="A6.F11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{{k_{X}^{+}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the input feature dimension <math id="A6.F11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{feat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{feat}</annotation></semantics></math> to normalize the <math id="A6.F11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance in the denominator.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
